@flexiarg cascade-fold/compile-when-path-is-clear
@title Compile the Cascade (when the construction is already evident)
@keywords cascade, fold, wiring, pipeline, compile, pure-function, dataflow, deterministic, construction, stage, selector, emit, terminals
@audience fold engineers, pattern composers
@tone constructive
@factor Equanimity (upekkha)
@style construction-strategy

! conclusion:
  When the construction for filling a hole is already evident, compile the cascade
  into a fixed pure-function pipeline (select rules -> match -> fold to fixpoint ->
  emit) and run it deterministically; surface undecidable obligations as policy-holes.

  + context: You hold a cascade of patterns that expresses how to fill a hole, and
    the construction path is ALREADY EVIDENT — you can see the decomposition into
    pure functions and the order in which they compose.

  + IF: You hold a cascade of patterns expressing how to fill a hole, and the
    construction path is already evident — you can see the decomposition into pure
    functions and the order in which they compose.

  + HOWEVER: The cascade is only correlation; until you commit to a decomposition and
    wire it, it stays inert prose. The danger is hard-coding one path when the path
    was not actually clear.
    + FAILURE-MODES:
        - The path only LOOKED clear because you were working backward from an answer
          you had already guessed; a pipeline then bakes in a confabulation.

  + THEN:
      1. Define the pure functions before the bang-verbs: selector, match, fold-step, emit.
      2. Assign each cascade contribution to a stage; warrant each stage by its pattern.
      3. Wire them as a linear dataflow; set the fixpoint / coverage-saturation stop.
      4. Emit the wiring with terminals = the sorry's (have, want); split undecidables out as policy-holes.

  + BECAUSE: When the construction is genuinely evident, the decomposition into pure
    functions and their composition order are already known, so a fixed deterministic
    pipeline meets the spec without the cost of searching a path you can already see.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
      - Define the pure functions (selector, match, fold-step, emit) before wiring the bang-verbs.
      - Warrant each stage by its cascade pattern and set the fixpoint / coverage-saturation stop.
      - Emit the wiring with terminals = the sorry's (have, want); split undecidables out as policy-holes.

  + QUALITY-CRITERIA:
      Well-applied: the construction was genuinely evident; every stage is warranted; terminals match the sorry.
      Badly-applied: used on an unclear path (should have searched); stages tagged post-hoc onto a pre-built answer.
